Given, $f(x+a y)+g(x-a y)=0$
differentiating w.r. to $x\begin{aligned}
& f^{\prime}(x+a y)\left(1+a y^{\prime}\right)+g^{\prime}(x-a y)(1-a y)=0 \\
& \Rightarrow a y^{\prime}\left(f^{\prime}(x+a y)-g^{\prime}(x-a y)+f(x+a y)+g^{\prime}(x-a y)=0\right. \\
& \Rightarrow a y^{\prime}=\frac{f^{\prime}(x+a y)+g^{\prime}(x-a y)}{g^{\prime}(x-a y)-f^{\prime}(x+a y)}
\end{aligned}$

